# Trivy ignore list — the ONLY escape hatch for the image CVE gate in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml ("Fail the build on HIGH/CRITICAL in the image").
#
# The gate already ignores advisories with no fixed version available
# (ignore-unfixed), so anything that reaches it CAN be fixed by bumping a
# dependency in pyproject.toml or the base-image digest in the Dockerfile.
# Prefer the bump. Dependabot watches pip, github-actions AND docker digests on
# the development branch, so the fix is usually already in a PR.
#
# Only add an id here when the bump is genuinely impossible right now, and give
# every entry all three of:
#   · the CVE / GHSA id
#   · WHY it does not apply or cannot be fixed yet
#   · a date to revisit and who owns it
# Entries are visible in the diff and in code review — that is the point. An
# undated entry is a permanently disabled control; treat one as a bug.
#
# Format: one id per line. Example (do not uncomment):
#   # CVE-0000-00000  libfoo — reachable only via the CLI we do not ship.
#   #                 Revisit 2026-12-01 (jhernandez); fixed upstream in 2.1.
#   CVE-0000-00000

# (empty — no exceptions in force)
